// Grenades: thrown equipment (Frag, Semtex, Proximity Mine, Flashbang, Stun Grenade, Smoke,
// Tear Gas) and the underslung launcher's round (Launcher). Read at startup from ./data/ (falls
// back to the copy built into the binary). The server flies each one as a physical projectile;
// clients draw it. Distances in metres, times in seconds, speeds in m/s. Which items a class can
// carry is data/class_points.ron, and the Level that unlocks each data/progression.ron.
//
//   speed, gravity   launch speed along the aim and the downward pull (game-tuned, not
//                    physical). For a thrown one `speed` is the cap: no throw may be faster
//                    (the client picks the speed by the look angle, the server clamps it)
//   throw            thrown ones only: how a throw leaves the hand by the look angle. A throw
//                    leaves lob_deg above the aim, at level_speed looking at the horizon. Looking
//                    up, the speed goes to up_speed and the lob fades out by up_pitch_deg above
//                    the horizon (farther and higher, 25-30 m at the horizon, about 40 m at 45
//                    degrees up). Looking down the speed falls to down_speed straight down
//                    (a short underhand toss, a few metres at 45 degrees down). A Grenade never
//                    leaves the hand steeper than max_launch_deg.
//   restitution      share of the speed into a surface kept when bouncing off it (a Grenade that
//                    sticks never bounces)
//   friction         share of the sideways speed kept on a bounce
//   radius           collision radius of the body
//   fuse             Timed(secs): bursts that long after leaving the hand;
//                    Impact(arm_distance, max_secs): bursts on the first surface it hits once it has
//                    flown arm_distance, or after max_secs in the air;
//                    Stick(secs, max_air_secs): sticks to the first surface or player it touches
//                    and bursts `secs` later (`max_air_secs` after leaving the hand if it touches
//                    nothing). On a player it rides along until they die, then drops;
//                    Proximity(arm_secs, trigger_radius, max_secs): a mine. Sticks to the first
//                    surface it touches (never a player), is armed `arm_secs` later and bursts
//                    when an enemy of its owner comes within trigger_radius in a clear line (or
//                    `max_secs` after the throw). A player keeps at most `count` of them down:
//                    placing one more removes their oldest
//   effect           Blast(damage, radius): `damage` at the centre, falling off linearly to nothing
//                    at `radius`, only to players it can reach in a straight line;
//                    Flash(radius, blind_secs, deaf_secs): blinds (white-out) players looking at it
//                    and deafens everyone, both fading with distance;
//                    Stun(radius, secs, slow): everyone within radius is shaken and slowed (by up to
//                    the share `slow`) for up to `secs`, fading with distance and weaker behind
//                    cover; no damage;
//                    Smoke(radius, secs): a cloud that blocks the view for `secs`;
//                    Gas(radius, secs, slow): a cloud that lasts `secs`; whoever stands in it
//                    coughs, is slowed (by up to the share `slow`) and sees a narrowed view,
//                    for a moment after leaving it too; no damage
//   count            how many a player carries (the Launcher's: rounds per life)
//   cooldown_secs    wait between two throws of the same kind (Launcher: between rounds)
{
    Frag: (
        name: "Frag Grenade",
        speed: 25.0,
        gravity: 14.0,
        restitution: 0.35,
        friction: 0.6,
        radius: 0.06,
        fuse: Timed(3.0),
        effect: Blast(damage: 150.0, radius: 8.0),
        count: 1,
        cooldown_secs: 1.0,
        throw: Some((
            lob_deg: 16.0,
            max_launch_deg: 70.0,
            down_speed: 3.0,
            level_speed: 25.0,
            up_speed: 23.0,
            up_pitch_deg: 45.0,
        )),
    ),
    Semtex: (
        name: "Semtex",
